BANKON — Licensing (dual, by component)
=======================================

BANKON is dual-licensed by component. The SPDX header in each source file is
authoritative; this file summarizes the split. Rationale: see POLICY.md.

1. CLIENT-FACING ENCRYPTION SOFTWARE  →  GNU GPLv3-or-later  (LICENSE.GPLv3)
   Code that generates keys or signs transactions — i.e. software users trust
   with their secrets:
     - bankon-waas/keygen.mjs
     - bankon-waas/sign.mjs
     - bankon-waas/public/offline-client.html
     - the in-browser keygen/signing in bankon-waas/public/index.html
   Like GnuPG (the GPL implementation of OpenPGP/PGP), cryptographic software
   that holds users' keys is kept copyleft so every derivative stays free and
   auditable. The "PGP is GPL" argument — see POLICY.md.

2. EVERYTHING ELSE  →  MIT  (LICENSE.MIT)
   Infrastructure, APIs, diagnostics, ops tooling — permissive to ease
   integration. None of it ever holds a user's private key or passphrase.

USER SOVEREIGNTY
----------------
Neither license, nor BANKON itself, asserts any control over your machine.
BANKON preserves your right to OWN YOUR FILESYSTEM and to do to your filesystem
anything you, as its owner, deem appropriate — install, modify, copy, delete,
inspect, relocate, or destroy any part of this software or its data. Your keys,
your device, your data, your rules. BANKON runs entirely on infrastructure you
control and never phones home. See POLICY.md.

